       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Single doses above about 1,000 mg are not typical. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily, or\n- Another dose?\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
